        "text": "PLANNING MESSAGE \u2014 Round 1, Grid Day 1, Block 1 (Night, base price 20)\n\nCurrent state: I have 0/10 MWh stored.\n\nSTRATEGY:\n- This block: CHARGE 9 MWh (to build storage).\n  - Why: The realized price formula is base - 2\u00d7(discharged - charged). If only I act, charging increases realized price by +2 per unit (base + 2x). At night (base 20), paying 20+2x per MWh is the cost. Discharging at peak (base 90) gives realized = 90-2x per unit. Net per unit \u2248 (90-2x)-(20+2x) = 70-4x. With 9 units: ~306 profit. This exceeds any alternative (e.g., charging at morning costs base 50 instead of 20).\n- Next blocks (assuming others hold): HOLD during morning and evening; DISCHARGE 9 MWh at peak (block 3).\n- Rationale: Charging at night is the cheapest base price. The realized-price adjustment favors charging low, discharging high. Discharging at peak maximizes per-unit realized price.\n- Key risk: If other owners also charge/discharge in the same block, the realized price adjusts and I may lose value. I'm assuming others will hold (neutral) \u2014 this is a baseline.\n\nNote: This is a planning phase. Final actions will be committed in the execution phase after block outcomes are published."
